<task id="034" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>spaarke_get_briefing and the Daily Briefing widget (ui://spaarke/briefing.html)</title>
    <phase>2 Long-running work, AI, widgets, task writes</phase>
    <gate>r1 gate RELEASED 2026-11-25 (joint mcp-r1/mcp-r2 determination under the owner's delegation; see notes/decisions.md D-r1-gate). Before starting, merge origin/master into this branch (merge, never rebase). Do not edit r1's ISS-010 files (DecisionCommitService, Actions/DecisionActionExecutors, RecordCreationService, CallerWriteAuthorization, CallerRecordAccessProbe, CallerMetadataReadMemo, AssignTaskNotifier, the email-bell job handler) or the Decision wizard heading files (DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx, Worklist/IssueLine.tsx, composeIssueLine.ts) without messaging mcp-r1 first.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF tool, new widget resource, embed and CI changes, React widget over a shared component</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows r1's widget scaffold (spaarke-decisions, DecisionsWidgetResource) and task 010's seam; the one open decision (which briefing call) has a bounded choice set</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>H</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>First of the serialised widget tasks (034 → 035 → 040 share McpModule.cs, Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj and publish-bff-artifact.yml); runs beside 030–033 and 036, which touch none of those</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010, 020, 021</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, ai, react, typescript, frontend, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add spaarke_get_briefing, returning the caller's AI Daily Briefing through the /api/ai/daily-briefing services (decide and record which call: render, narrate or summarize, matching what the Console shows), with a short text summary for the model and the full payload in structuredContent; and a single-file widget src/client/widgets/spaarke-briefing/ that renders DailyBriefingApp through task 010's injected data service over task 021's shared transport, served as ui://spaarke/briefing.html through McpModule with an empty CSP and embedded by the publish workflow. If generation can exceed 30 s, use McpLongRunning.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in MCP Apps widgets, Fluent v9 and the Daily Briefing pipeline.</role>
  <goal>The tool returns the same briefing the Console shows the same user that day; the widget renders it in Chat and Cowork in light and dark; the Console and standalone Daily Briefing tests pass unchanged; the bundle is &lt; 1 MB target, ≤ 3 MB hard.</goal>

  <context>
