  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 010, 020, 021; find the call the Console makes for the briefing and record the decision (render/narrate/summarize, ≤ 30 s or long-running) in notes/decisions.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Write GetBriefingTool (and the app-only data tool if needed), BriefingWidgetResource, McpModule registration, ledger rows and the contract test.</step>
    <step order="3">Scaffold spaarke-briefing from spaarke-decisions; render DailyBriefingApp with the injected service over the shared transport; write App.test.tsx; build and run check-bundle-size.mjs.</step>
    <step order="4">Add the csproj embed and the publish-bff-artifact.yml steps; verify a local publish embeds briefing.html.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the Daily Briefing package tests, MCP suites, ArchTests and conformance; measure the publish-size delta (the embedded HTML counts).</step>
    <step order="6">Write the proposed CAPABILITY-INDEX row into notes/capability-index-pending.md.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Console's briefing comes from more than one call and no single call reproduces it, STOP and present the options (spec Unresolved Question) to the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the bundle exceeds 3 MB, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>DailyBriefingApp (Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components) with 010's seam; /api/ai/daily-briefing services; r1's widget scaffold and DecisionsWidgetResource; notes/reuse-scan.md rows "Daily Briefing component" and "Widget resource".</existing>
    <extension>The component, services and scaffold are reused; the new resource class and widget folder are required because each MCP App widget is a separate single-file ui:// resource (owner Q5: one Console component per widget).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Copilot users cannot see their Daily Briefing, and FR-09/FR-16's widget acceptance fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Briefing widget in Copilot Chat and Cowork">
      <steps>
        <step>After deploy 039, ask "What's my Spaarke daily briefing?" in Copilot Chat with the Spaarke MCP source</step>
        <step>Verify the widget renders the same TL;DR and sections the Console shows the same user that day</step>
        <step>Repeat in Cowork; tab through the widget with the keyboard</step>
        <step>Check the widget console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Same briefing as the Console; keyboard operable; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds and text follow the host theme; no hard-coded colours</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens only</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
    <tool name="npm">build, jest and check-bundle-size in src/client/widgets/spaarke-briefing</tool>
  </tools>

